     Sharpe is -15.218 — every cell in this batch is deeply negative. When a
     pool is uniformly bad, E[max SR] is dragged down with it and a merely LESS
     catastrophic config can post a high-looking DSR while losing money on every
     trade. The DSR column below is therefore NOT informative in this batch, and
     it is not doing any work: SURVIVOR requires net PF > 1 AND Sharpe > 0 as well,
     and both of those bind long before DSR does. Do not quote a DSR from this run
     as evidence of anything.

  RUIN DIAGNOSTICS at the repo's 1% risk/trade convention: 3/30 cells have a day losing >= 100% of equity (which would invalidate maxDD);
  30/30 cells end with equity below 1% of its start. maxDD and the
  equity curve are LEVERAGE-DEPENDENT and 1%/trade x ~25 trades/day is not a
  realistic sizing. Sharpe IS leverage-invariant (mu/sigma cancels the scale), and
  so are gross PF, net PF, cost_R and R/trade. The verdict rests on those.

